   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Tundra wolf sleeping in the grass at the Alaska Wildlife Conservation Center in Girdwood, Alaska. The tundra wolf is a subspecies of the gray wolf. The AWCC is a wildlife sanctuary that provides a permanent home for animals that were either abandoned at a young age or injured in the wild. The AWCC cares for the animals that are unable to survive in the wild on their own.</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
